From a1450a48afa045de03269bec8db57b7ba8ced61e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <dev@example.com>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 14:48:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: WhatsApp data-purchase bot via Cloud API webhook

Lets a user buy data, and now also fund their wallet, by chatting the
WhatsApp Business number instead of opening the app. Reuses the existing
wallet debit/refund, wallet-funding, and Alrahuz provider logic
end-to-end - no purchase/money code is duplicated.

- prisma: add WhatsAppSession (per-phone conversation state), RLS enabled
  to match the rest of the schema
- config/env.ts: WHATSAPP_TOKEN, WHATSAPP_PHONE_NUMBER_ID,
  WHATSAPP_VERIFY_TOKEN, WHATSAPP_APP_SECRET (all optional)
- routes/vtu.routes.ts: export processProviderPurchase so the bot uses the
  exact same debit -> provider call -> refund-on-failure sequence as the
  REST /data/purchase endpoint
- routes/webhook.routes.ts:
  - GET /api/webhooks/whatsapp verification handshake + POST
    /api/webhooks/whatsapp inbound messages, signature verified via
    X-Hub-Signature-256 the same way the Paystack webhook verifies
    x-paystack-signature
  - Paystack handler now sends a WhatsApp confirmation once a
    WhatsApp-initiated funding transaction is credited, since the
    existing in-app push notification won't be seen by someone who paid
    entirely from WhatsApp
- services/whatsapp-session.service.ts: menu-number-driven state machine
  (network -> plan -> recipient -> PIN -> confirm), plus a global "fund"
  command (works from any state, like "cancel") that collects an amount,
  reuses createPendingFunding + paystackService.initializeTransaction
  exactly like POST /wallet/fund, and texts back the Paystack checkout
  link. Data-purchase amounts are re-fetched by plan ID at confirmation
  time rather than trusting the cached session amount, and the purchase's
  idempotency key is the WhatsApp message ID so a redelivered webhook can
  never double-charge

Not yet done, left for a follow-up: an admin-panel view of
WhatsAppSession for support, and a "balance" command to check wallet
balance without starting a purchase.
